  <Properties>
    <articleTitle>
      <Value Culture="en"><![CDATA[ Volkswagen ID. Cross officially announced. Three engines to choose from. They'll definitely play on price.]]></Value>
      <Value Culture="pl-PL"><![CDATA[Volkswagen ID. Cross oficjalnie. Trzy silniki do wyboru. Na pewno zagrają tu ceną]]></Value>
    </articleTitle>
    <author>
      <Value><![CDATA[umb://document/833364f91e1e4f9a866584920b87dfba]]></Value>
    </author>
    <components>
      <Value Culture="en"><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "bc8cfc9b-08fe-4be1-8a61-49c6dedf32ba",
      "key": "ce792ed4-417a-4361-83ad-776d71e90bf1",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "componentText",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe Volkswagen ID. Polo has just been joined by a small SUV based on it. Officially meet the new Volkswagen ID. Cross. This electric model has a lot riding on it \u2013 it\u0027s expected to win over the unconvinced with an attractive price.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EAfter years of announcements and promises, Volkswagen has finally entered the small, affordable electric vehicle segment. Small but spacious cars based on the MEB\u002B platform will soon hit the roads. Volkswagen will have two such ID. Polo and ID. Cross models, with Skoda, Cupra, and Audi also having or planning to have equivalents. Will they really be affordable? Volkswagen has priced the base version of the ID. Polo at PLN 99,000.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "settingsData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "c350d716-b434-45f7-a645-6176f4fb7c2d",
      "key": "b2f612b8-6848-4c13-8650-9a84a1393f86",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "hideBlockElement",
          "culture": null,
